## Coordinate and stopping theorem

Define a directed spline coordinate \(s\) increasing along the selected route.

Use the front coupler only for stopping:

\[
x = s_{\text{target}} - s_{\text{front coupler}}
\]

\[
v_s = \frac{d s_{\text{front coupler}}}{dt}.
\]

The stopping theorem applies only when \(x>0\) and \(v_s>0\). Wrong-way motion, target crossing, unavailable route orientation, or invalid localization must enter recovery or fail closed.

Support either physical/world orientation by selecting the appropriate directed spline orientation, but do not accept a station approach that conflicts with its configured direction.

